{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head `8389df6fc1cc7ffb45c7bdc228061043295dfafc`, on main `d56394da`. No person and no desktop AI app has seen these words, and finding 6 rests on a measurement from a screenshot, because the fixture draws no Reply box. So the next person's session must check finding 6.\n\n**Finding 1, the defect.** The new words state the lane's rule. I compared `mergeHolds` with the guards of `acts.merge` in `apps/room/lanes/src/change.ts` and `change-finding.ts`: `not-complete`, `merge-in-progress`, `rules-unknown`, `approvals-needed`, `changes-requested`, `required-check-not-passed` and `finding-open`. The conditions match, including the manifest binding of a review and a check's configuration. `changeActions` now uses the same function, so the Merge button and the row cannot disagree. The real-scope trace in `change-view.scope.test.ts` passes, and the holds control fails by its assertion. `versionOf` counts `current` and `superseded`, the manifest's only two states, so it agrees with the card's `context.versions`.\n\n**Finding 5, the first card.** This is where a press could go wrong, so I read the path.\n\n- `checked` lets a first card keep its acts only with `wholeText`, and it refuses `wholeText` without a body.\n- The browser draws the body before the acts, and it never cuts the body. A longer text shows no act.\n- The press takes the same `at` and `bodyAt` as the opened card, so an old first card gets `revision-moved` or `stale-question`.\n- After an unknown outcome, a whole-text first card offers only the check of the original, also after paging away and back.\n\nYour two controls that first survived, logs 31 and 56, stay on record, and logs 33 and 58 fail by their assertions.\n\n**The other findings.**\n\n- **Finding 2.** The row now sits in a closed disclosure as a text node.\n- **Finding 3.** The J5 log shows two cards with different titles and lines.\n- **Finding 4.** `receiptLine` gives a person the `done` words only for an accepted act. The model's context keeps the entry through `exactReceipt`, and it uses that text only while the receipt is the same line.\n- **Finding 7.** The empty words depend on the screen, and a cut list says what it did not read.\n- **Rule lines, `219ba382`.** A person reads words, and the digest and clause stay in the row, the record and the Page's **Exact rule**. J5's \"names its rule\" still holds through that disclosure.\n\n**Next edit, not blocking.** The settles line tells a person that a reviewer can replace a verdict with a new review, and the card offers no act for that: a viewer who has reviewed is no longer `reviewable`, and a person needs the ordinary act tool with `earlier`. The sentence is true of the lane, and your note says so. It still sits against the rule from the card's press, that a person is not told to do what the card offers no way to do. Either offer the act or say where it is done. The planner can place that.\n\n**Evidence.** Both units verify, `SHA256SUMS` `e3030b8d…` and `77fcabab…`, with no writable file. `gate/gate.exit` says exit 0 at `f57299c9`, and from there to this head only notes, manifests and the report differ. `gh` shows card run 41355997652 succeeded at `90408884`. I compared `90408884..8389df6fc1cc7ffb45c7bdc228061043295dfafc` with this head's card workflow paths, and no path matches, so the rule in `0998f9ec` holds for the card's bytes. The workflow's new paths, `apps/views/src/**` and `card-words.ts`, close a gap that this head's words would have fallen through. Page run 41356120831 succeeded at `f57299c9`.\n\nAt this head I ran `apps/views` tests (34 passed), `view-sessions` and `page-needs-you` (23 passed), `change-view.scope.test.ts` (19 passed), the Page's `assets` test (1 passed) and the seal test (10 passed). `check-notes`, `check-doc-links` (1006 links, 0 broken) and `check-commit-messages` pass, and the worktree is clean. I did not rerun the browser script.\n\n**Architecture.** One function now states what holds a merge, for the row and the button. It restates the lane's guards in code, and the trace is what keeps them together, so a future guard needs both. `kicker`, `record`, `rule`, `done` and `wholeText` are optional card fields, so a declared card keeps its behaviour.\n\n**Security.** No authority moves. A first-card act signs what the opened card signed, and the scope judges it. The row's JSON holds what the old body held. The page renders text as text.\n\n**Simplification.** `mergeHolds` removes the card's second copy of the merge test. `RULE_WORDS` is a small table with a fallback, which is enough.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7ddfc7e8b2276f06202c65ef0641cc13a855942e","binding":"assigned","head":"8389df6fc1cc7ffb45c7bdc228061043295dfafc","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3f2fc32763d66b5df8943dade66cc1e90fc2c6b0\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:958f632c038416f8349894d203b774d2bc1017c9\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7429691804ded1c46f9bac1cc0441088bcafc8f9","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}